\section{NVE Threshold Sensitivity Analysis}
\label{sec:appendix_sensitivity}

We report the full sensitivity analysis for the NVE diagnostic framework introduced in Section~\ref{sec:results}. The main text reports Task~B2 (any CIVO detection, $\nve \geq 1.5\times$). Here we additionally present Task~B1, which restricts the positive class to \emph{sustained} CIVO, specifically experiments exhibiting persistent, accelerating value overestimation that progresses to performance collapse. Transient CIVO cases (e.g., exp~009b, which self-corrects after a brief excursion above the threshold) are classified as negative in B1.

\subsection{Per-Experiment NVE Values}

Table~\ref{tab:nve_raw} lists the NVE values at 35K+ training steps for all eight factorial experiments. Experiments are sorted by descending NVE. Experiment 008e\_v3\_s2 exhibits elevated NVE ($3.78\times$) due to Imagination-Reality Divergence (IRD), a mechanistically distinct phenomenon from CIVO, and is classified as negative in both tasks.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Per-experiment NVE values (35K+ steps) and ground truth labels. $+$ = positive (CIVO), $-$ = negative. IRD = Imagination-Reality Divergence; trans.\ = transient CIVO with self-correction.}
\label{tab:nve_raw}
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}lrccc@{}}
\toprule
Experiment & NVE & Mechanism & B1 & B2 \\
\midrule
006          & 4.84 & sustained CIVO & $+$ & $+$ \\
008d         & 4.13 & sustained CIVO & $+$ & $+$ \\
008e\_v3\_s2 & 3.78 & IRD (non-CIVO) & $-$ & $-$ \\
009b         & 1.62 & transient CIVO & $-$ & $+$ \\
001          & 1.00 & non-CIVO       & $-$ & $-$ \\
008f         & 0.97 & non-CIVO       & $-$ & $-$ \\
008e\_v3\_s1 & 0.94 & non-CIVO       & $-$ & $-$ \\
008a         & 0.93 & non-CIVO       & $-$ & $-$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection{Multi-Threshold Classification Performance}

